public import CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterB.Section01.ComponentRecognition.SylowOvergroups.SmallModels

/-!
# Model Sylow restrictions for B.1.13

The reductions use the actual conjugation image in Aut(L), the restricted
Sylow subgroup, and the relative subnormality in K ∨ T. Proper Sylow
overgroups retain the central factor in the bound F*(X) ≤ O₂(X)(X ∩ Z(L)).

The binary PSL₂ and A₅ automorphism restrictions, and the complete A₅
subgroup conclusion, are proved. The remaining characteristic-two models,
the triple cover of A₆, and the arbitrary-degree alternating overgroup
classification still require model calculations. This module does not
assert the full source theorem while those inputs remain undischarged.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined 1 March 2004 manuscript, B.1.13,
printed p.74 (PDF p.85).
-/
